      "mergeID": "614915c5921d1c67f673a807",
      "mergedPostDetails": "VRCSDK3 2020.12.09.04.44\nI've tried to make a script that when the head of a player goes inside a wall it will activate a sphere that blinds them and it checks if the collider is a trigger or not, to prevent triggers to activate it. Everything works alright, until I discover that if you have an avatar with a VRC Station in it, if the head goes inside that collider no matter if you check if the collider is null, it will always return an NullReferenceException. To be more precise, the node that's throwing the error is \"get isTrigger\". From various tests, I've discovered that the collider doesn't return null, I can see the name of the object and what type of collision is, in the moment I try to get the isTrigger or any other thing (like \"get Gameobject\"), even if I try to Null check it, it will always return an error. I've tried to set a variable after the onTriggerEnter and use that instead, but same result.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "OnTriggerEnter with isTrigger breaks when enter VRC Station of an avatar",
